        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/69888?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">adding a new guide.<br>\nOther guide is <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3838773711\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42853\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42853/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42853\">#42853</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43587",
            "title": "New guide: animation timeline range insets",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-31T08:03:31.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-26T15:27:57.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "estelle",
                "url": "https://github.com/estelle"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds reference docs for WebAssembly SIMD arithmetic instructions (and possibly some more bitwise ones too).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note: I've updated the general <code class=\"notranslate\">shl</code> page to cover SIMD and non-SIMD values. I've also deleted the previously published SIMD-specific <code class=\"notranslate\">shl</code> page and redirected it to the general one.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43583",
            "title": "Document Wasm SIMD arithmetic instructions",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-26T17:53:39.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-26T11:55:34.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/56009637?u=2c59626cda2ec34a16e55d6071ceaffb1698a34a&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Applies the css invert to the item in the example labelled <code class=\"notranslate\">invert() filter</code> instead of the SVG invert for the <code class=\"notranslate\">SVG filter equivalent</code>, and fixes the SVG filter equivalent with a class as the document's text explains rather than as an inline SVG.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The changes keep the content accurate and make the playground more useable.</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43581",
            "title": "Changes example in CSS invert() to use appropriate classes.",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-26T20:57:21.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-26T02:25:13.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "elooly10",
                "url": "https://github.com/elooly10"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Between versions 142 and 145, Chrome enables support for various features of the <a href=\"https://wicg.github.io/local-network-access/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Local Network Access spec</a>. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5152728072060928\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5152728072060928</a> and <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5068298146414592\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5068298146414592</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Specifically, these are:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">targetAddressSpace</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">Request</code> property, and the equivalent <code class=\"notranslate\">RequestInit</code> property.</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">local-network-access</code> permission/<code class=\"notranslate\">Permissions-Policy</code> directive.</li>\n<li>The more granular <code class=\"notranslate\">local-network</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">loopback-network</code> permissions/<code class=\"notranslate\">Permissions-Policy</code> directives.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Adds reference pages for the above features.</li>\n<li>Adds a new \"Local network access\" guide inside the MDN security section (I didn't add a regular API page for this, because it doesn't really feel like it warrants an API page — it is just a single property and some new permissions, in terms of web developer footprint.)</li>\n<li>Adds links to the guide from several related places.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43575",
            "title": "Technical review: Document local network access",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-27T14:03:10.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-25T15:14:24.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/227569687?u=4d080a52f318b27812ffeaac93b306fff32403d3&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This PR fixes a misleading sentence in the dispatchEvent() documentation.</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Changes made:</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Converted the return value description into a clear and complete sentence</li>\n<li>Improved readability for beginners</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Result:</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The behavior of dispatchEvent() return value is now easier to understand.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43525.\">Closes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4118052510\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43525\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43525/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43525\">#43525</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Proof of change: ISSUE (false if event is cancelable, and at least one of the event handlers which received event called Event.preventDefault(). Otherwise true.)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">(Screenshot attach here)</p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/227569687/568240591-876e9fa9-4192-4361-befd-c7ce6da5ccee.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3NzUwMjIxODgsIm5iZiI6MTc3NTAyMTg4OCwicGF0aCI6Ii8yMjc1Njk2ODcvNTY4MjQwNTkxLTg3NmU5ZmE5LTQxOTItNDM2MS1iZWZkLWM3Y2U2ZGE1Y2NlZS5wbmc_.ywFgjD-VuVmidkJ1GGns-ArehWBhJrYYj60-SKo40Dg\"><img width=\"554\" height=\"144\" alt=\"Screenshot from 2026-03-24 14-31-16\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/227569687/568240591-876e9fa9-4192-4361-befd-c7ce6da5ccee.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3NzUwMjIxODgsIm5iZiI6MTc3NTAyMTg4OCwicGF0aCI6Ii8yMjc1Njk2ODcvNTY4MjQwNTkxLTg3NmU5ZmE5LTQxOTItNDM2MS1iZWZkLWM3Y2U2ZGE1Y2NlZS5wbmc_.ywFgjD-VuVmidkJ1GGns-ArehWBhJrYYj60-SKo40Dg\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 144px;\"></a>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/227569687/568241200-f0c565d0-bccb-48b1-a4c7-5f573a63e908.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3NzUwMjIxODgsIm5iZiI6MTc3NTAyMTg4OCwicGF0aCI6Ii8yMjc1Njk2ODcvNTY4MjQxMjAwLWYwYzU2NWQwLWJjY2ItNDhiMS1hNGM3LTVmNTczYTYzZTkwOC5wbmc_.10vNNdwuunS8EKDnj4Ed47WxACuobXV3tr5MQx5mmhA\"><img width=\"1299\" height=\"691\" alt=\"Screenshot from 2026-03-24 14-32-20\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/227569687/568241200-f0c565d0-bccb-48b1-a4c7-5f573a63e908.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3NzUwMjIxODgsIm5iZiI6MTc3NTAyMTg4OCwicGF0aCI6Ii8yMjc1Njk2ODcvNTY4MjQxMjAwLWYwYzU2NWQwLWJjY2ItNDhiMS1hNGM3LTVmNTczYTYzZTkwOC5wbmc_.10vNNdwuunS8EKDnj4Ed47WxACuobXV3tr5MQx5mmhA\" style=\"max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 691px;\"></a>",
