        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF149 added support for <code class=\"notranslate\">referenceTarget</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">shadowRootReferenceTarget</code> attributes behind a pref. These are already mostly documented in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3711686776\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/42323\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/42323/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/42323\">#42323</a>. This is pretty basic, but it was and remains about the right level because this isnt supported in releases or preview yet. At that point we should create guide material and cross link (this can be generated from the <a href=\"https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/blob/gh-pages/proposals/reference-target-explainer.md\">explainer</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">What this does is get us a little bit closer so that when we have to update there is less to do.</p>\n<ol dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Update the docs to use correct templates</li>\n<li>Add linked individual property property docs rather than just the top level doc.</li>\n</ol>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I have put a little bit more work into <code class=\"notranslate\">ShadowRoot.referenceTarget</code> docs because it ONLY affects this property. So we could in theory add examples and so on to this without being confusing for other docs. See inline comments.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4080141592\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43453\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43453/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43453\">#43453</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43543",
            "title": "FF149 ShadowRoot referenceTarget and friends minor update",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-24T07:09:59.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-24T06:54:06.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome 145 adds support for the <code class=\"notranslate\">PerformanceNavigationTiming.confidence</code> property, and the associated <code class=\"notranslate\">PerformanceTimingConfidence</code> interface. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5186950448283648\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5186950448283648</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds documentation for both features mentioned above.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n\n\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43528",
            "title": "Editorial review: Document PerformanceNavigationTiming.confidence",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-31T10:14:40.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-23T09:56:02.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/646274?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Clarified the difference between native events and manually dispatched events in the dispatchEvent documentation.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The previous phrasing implied that the actual event handler functions themselves are scheduled asynchronously on the Event Loop, but only the dispatch is.</p>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Additional details</h3>\n\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Related issues and pull requests</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/EventTarget/dispatchEvent\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/EventTarget/dispatchEvent</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #43519.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4117119113\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43519\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43519/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43519\">#43519</a></p>\n\n\n\n",
